  "resolution": {
    "reason": "Not a defect in wallet-backend. Its participant table (docs/architecture/state-changes.md, at e967ce8b and 3e22515a) lists 'Accounts named in the operation body, for example payment destinations, claimants, trustors, and clawback holders' as participants of successful transactions. Recording a claimant of a claimable balance as a participant is therefore wallet-backend's documented definition; it stores no state change or movement for such an account. The difference comes from this kit's stricter rule. The entries keep their expectation and the cells are declared.",
    "reviewer": "kit-maintainer",
    "date": "2026-11-18",
    "manifest_action": "divergence recorded as wont_fix on the five entries (stellar/wallet-backend e967ce8b and 3e22515a), naming this record"
  },
